==Irish==
{{wikipedia|lang=ga}}

===Etymology===
Specific use of {{m|ga|béarla|t=speech, language}}, from {{der|ga|sga|bélrae}}, from {{m|sga|bél|t=mouth}}. Compare {{cog|gd|Beurla Ghallta}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Munster}} {{IPA|ga|/ˈbʲiːa̯ɾˠl̪ˠə/}}
* {{a|Connacht}} {{IPA|ga|/ˈbʲeːɾˠl̪ˠə/}}
* {{a|Ulster}} {{IPA|ga|/ˈbʲeːɾˠl̪ˠə/|[ˈbʲɛːɾˠl̪ˠə]}}

===Proper noun===
{{ga-proper noun|m|~}}

# [[English]] {{gloss|language}}
#: {{ux|ga|Is fearr Gaeilge bhriste ná '''Béarla''' cliste.|Broken Irish is better than clever '''English'''.|q=proverb}}

====Usage notes====
The definite article is not always used with this noun.

